    "description": "AccountLockoutPolicy tests need users with precise combinations of failed attempts, last-failure timestamps, trusted-device flags, and recovery status. The constructor rejects invalid combinations, and most tests care about only one or two values while the remaining fields merely establish a legitimate starting account. Create a type-specific setup API in the security test support package that begins with a valid locked-account baseline and lets each test vary only the relevant property, such as failedAttemptCount or lastFailureAt. Tests must still read as explicit examples of account state, and the setup API must enforce the same cross-field constraints as production code. It should not expose dozens of unrelated constructor arguments, and it should not be used by production code.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose a type-specific test setup API that supplies valid account defaults while each lockout test states only the security condition it verifies.",
    "notes": "Lockout tests build on a type-specific setup API with a valid baseline and vary only the asserted property (test-data-builder); object-mother is the near-miss for the shared-baseline dimension."
